    <string name="rules_title">Rules</string>
    <string name="rules_1">Tap a pit on your row. The stones go counterclockwise, one per pit, into your store too, skipping theirs.</string>
    <string name="rules_2">Last stone lands in your store? Go again.</string>
    <string name="rules_3">Last stone lands in an empty pit on your side? That stone and everything across from it go to your store.</string>
    <string name="rules_ex1">Unless the pit across is empty. Then nothing.</string>
    <string name="rules_ex2">When one row is empty, the other player sweeps their leftovers into their store. More stones wins.</string>
    <string name="mistakes_title">Common slips</string>
    <string name="mistake_1">Count first: n stones means the last one lands n pits away. The preview shows you.</string>
    <string name="mistake_2">One stone in the pit next to your store? That\'s a free extra turn.</string>
    <string name="mistake_3">Don\'t empty your pits too early. Empty pits are capture bait.</string>
    <string name="mistake_4">Their row almost empty? Keep yours light. Whatever you have left goes to them.</string>
    <string name="rules_start">Start</string>
    <string name="rules_diagram">Your row a–f, your store on the right, theirs F–A on the far side.</string>

